{"html":"<p>What does this print?</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">console.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">log</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"1\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">setTimeout</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(() </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> console.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">log</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"2\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">), </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">0</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">Promise</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">resolve</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">().</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">then</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(() </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> console.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">log</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"3\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">));</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">console.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">log</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"4\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>The answer is <code>1</code>, <code>4</code>, <code>3</code>, <code>2</code>. If that surprises you, the event loop explains it, and once you know its few rules, you can predict any order like this one.</p>\n<h2 id=\"one-thread-one-thing-at-a-time\">One Thread, One Thing at a Time</h2>\n<p>JavaScript in a browser tab runs your code on a single thread. It can only do one thing at a time. Yet pages fetch data, wait for clicks and run timers all at once. The trick: the slow waiting happens <em>outside</em> JavaScript, in the browser, and JavaScript only runs the short callbacks when the results are ready.</p>\n<p>Four parts make this work:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The call stack:</strong> the functions running right now.</li>\n<li><strong>Web APIs</strong> (or Node&#39;s equivalents): timers, network requests and events, handled by the browser while your code keeps going.</li>\n<li><strong>The task queue:</strong> callbacks waiting to run, like timers and clicks. Also called the macrotask queue.</li>\n<li><strong>The microtask queue:</strong> a second, higher-priority queue, for promise callbacks and <code>queueMicrotask</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"the-rules\">The Rules</h2>\n<p>The event loop repeats these steps:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Run the current task until the call stack is empty.</li>\n<li>Run <strong>every</strong> microtask in the microtask queue, including new ones added while running them.</li>\n<li>Let the browser render, if it&#39;s time to update the screen.</li>\n<li>Take the <strong>next one</strong> task from the task queue, and go back to step 1.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The key difference: after each task, <em>all</em> microtasks run, but only <em>one</em> task runs per turn.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-example-step-by-step\">The Example, Step by Step</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><code>console.log(&quot;1&quot;)</code> runs: prints <code>1</code>.</li>\n<li><code>setTimeout</code> hands the callback to the browser&#39;s timer. After 0 ms, the callback goes into the <strong>task</strong> queue.</li>\n<li><code>.then</code> puts its callback in the <strong>microtask</strong> queue, because the promise is already resolved.</li>\n<li><code>console.log(&quot;4&quot;)</code> runs: prints <code>4</code>.</li>\n<li>The script is done and the stack is empty. Microtasks run first: prints <code>3</code>.</li>\n<li>The next task runs, the timer callback: prints <code>2</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><code>setTimeout(fn, 0)</code> doesn&#39;t mean &quot;now&quot;. It means &quot;as a new task, after the current one and all microtasks&quot;. Browsers also wait at least 4 ms for timers nested more than five levels deep.</p>\n<h2 id=\"where-async-await-fits\">Where async/await Fits</h2>\n<p><code>await</code> is promise syntax. Everything after an <code>await</code> runs as a microtask once the awaited value is ready:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">async</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> load</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  console.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">log</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"A\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  await</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> null</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  console.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">log</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"B\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">load</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">console.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">log</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"C\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>This prints <code>A</code>, <code>C</code>, <code>B</code>. The function runs synchronously until the first <code>await</code>, then returns. <code>B</code> runs later, as a microtask, after the rest of the current code.</p>\n<h2 id=\"why-a-long-loop-freezes-the-page\">Why a Long Loop Freezes the Page</h2>\n<p>While a task runs, nothing else can: no clicks, no rendering, no other callbacks.</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">button.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">addEventListener</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"click\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, () </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> end</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> Date.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">now</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 3000</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  while</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (Date.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">now</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> end) {} </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// busy for 3 seconds</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">});</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>For three seconds the page doesn&#39;t respond, and the screen doesn&#39;t update. The same happens with an endless chain of microtasks, which never lets the loop reach the render step.</p>\n<p>To stay responsive, split long work into smaller tasks, move it to a Web Worker, which runs on another thread, or use <code>await</code> on real asynchronous work like <code>fetch</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"rendering-and-requestanimationframe\">Rendering and requestAnimationFrame</h2>\n<p>The browser renders between tasks, typically 60 times a second. <code>requestAnimationFrame(callback)</code> runs your callback right before the next render, which makes it the right place for animations: changes made there show in the very next frame.</p>\n<h2 id=\"a-harder-example\">A Harder Example</h2>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">console.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">log</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"start\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">setTimeout</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(() </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  console.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">log</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"timeout\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">  Promise</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">resolve</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">().</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">then</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(() </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> console.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">log</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"promise inside timeout\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">));</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">0</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">Promise</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">resolve</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">()</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  .</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">then</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(() </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> console.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">log</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"promise 1\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">))</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  .</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">then</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(() </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> console.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">log</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"promise 2\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">));</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">console.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">log</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"end\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>The output:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>start</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>end</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>promise 1</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>promise 2</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>timeout</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>promise inside timeout</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p><code>promise 2</code> is queued only when <code>promise 1</code> finishes, but it still runs before the timer, because the loop empties the microtask queue completely, new microtasks included. The promise inside the timer runs right after that timer&#39;s task ends.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-about-node-js\">What About Node.js?</h2>\n<p>Node uses the same idea with a few extra queues. Microtasks still run after each callback, and <code>process.nextTick</code> callbacks run even before promise microtasks. The order of <code>setTimeout(fn, 0)</code> and <code>setImmediate</code> can vary in the main script, but inside an I/O callback <code>setImmediate</code> always runs first.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-rules-in-short\">The Rules in Short</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Synchronous code runs first, to the end.</li>\n<li>Then every microtask: promise callbacks, code after <code>await</code>, <code>queueMicrotask</code>.</li>\n<li>Then the browser may render.</li>\n<li>Then one task: a timer, an event, a message.</li>\n<li>A long task or an endless microtask chain blocks everything, including the screen.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>To see these queues move, step through the examples in the <a href=\"/visualizers/javascript-event-loop/\">event loop visualizer</a>.</p>\n"}